
1.Understand <!DOCTYPE>, <html>, <head>, <body>. Create a simple HTML page.
	
	<!DOCTYPE> - this defines Document type is html
	<html> - Html - hyper text markup language, it is used to create web layouts.
		 html tag is root tag, this contains head, body and footer tags.
	<head> - head tag contain title tag and meta tags.
		 title tag is used to define title name for webpage, it helps SEO(search engine optimization) 
		   -for understand what our webpage is about.
	<body> - body tag contains header, main and footer tags and many more. it contains all the visible content of webpage.

Create a simple HTML page:-
		
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Document</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1> Hello World! </h1>
    <p> Welcome to my html page </p>
</body>
</html>

 
	
2.Explore the root element <html>. Learn how it wraps the entire document.

	HTML - all the tags are called elements, html is root element of html webpage, it wraps all the tags in entire html document
	html - root element
	head - information about webpage
	body - visible content
	
	<html>  - root element
	<head>	
		<title> </title>
	</head>
	<body> 
	</body>
	</html>

